! S22 Mag tape routines
%endoflist
%include "subarc:ssownf3"
%list

! 1 jun 87
! failure in 'mag' routines now gives a signalevent 12,1 instead of monitorstop
! allowing for possible tidy up by calling prog.
! fix in magio at read fixed to allow for a short final block and hence record
! 22 jan 86
! fix in 'open tape' for mode=either, and holding a 'hold' across a release
! for a mode change
! 6-aug-85
! revisited for Amdahl
!
! 2-MAR-83:
!     'TAPE ALREADY CLAIMED' INCLUDED AS ERROR 23
!     AND CHECKED FOR AFTER 'OPEN TAPE' IN 'CHECK TAPE'
!     VOL1 INCLUDED WITH EOF1 IN LOCATE T(9/10) TO INDICATE EOT RATHER THAN
!     EMPTY FILE. THIS CATERS FOR EMPTY TAPES.
!     CC==NOT SET ON ENTRY TO MAGIO, TO MAKE THE TEST AT SOPEND: SIMPLE
!     FLAG<1 FOLLOWING 'OPEN TAPE' IN 'CHECK TAPE' (IE ALREADY ALLOCATED)
!     DROPS THROUGH TO SET UP CF_CHANNEL AND CC CORRECTLY BEFORE RETURNING
!     WITH FLAG=0.
!     'OPERATION' INCLUDED IN FAILURE MESS IN MAGIO, AND %MONITOR REMOVED.
! 24-FEB-83: CDM
!     Service routines:-
!        OPEN TAPE - _term flag set=yes as default
!        LOCATE - extra check at t(3) and t(4) for first skip ok.
!                 fix for t(8)
!                 t(9) and t(10), flag=4 only forward. -4 return removed.
!        SKIP BLOCKS - fix for _block no when 0 or 4.

!     Magio:-
!        check for channel ptr=0 on entry, to cater for close after failure
!        during open before channel allocation.
!        OPEN TAPE FILE - null dsn disallowed for write and write-mod in sl mode
!                         EOT in physical mode prepositioning for write OK.
!                         _term flag=NO delayed until all opening complete.
!                         fix for type(11),  TSFO+100.
!        CHECK TAPE - flag=73 now 90 for 'too many tapes'.
!                     cf_channel allocated before possible tsfo+10 return to
!                     ensure we deallocate on a subsequebt close.
!                     checking for _init fsn redone. TSFO+1 only if invalid
!                     header successfully read. flag 1 or 4 allowed tpo proceed.
!        FIND FILE - physical mode does skip block look-ahead after locate, to
!                    catch EOT. locate beyond EOT gives TSFO+16 insetad of EOF.
!        VALIDATE FOR READ/WRITE - _term flag not set.
!
!     Support routines:-
!        flags 2 and 3 for catastrophe.
!        advise to change from MT to MAG routines.
!

!**********************************************************************

!            MAG  TAPE INTERFACE ROUTINES 1ST JUNE

!**********************************************************************

!     1. service routines.
!     2. HLL interface routines.
!     3. Support routines. MT and MAG.
!     4. DEFINEMT and FORTRAN interface.
!

!  THE MAIN PURPOSE OF IMPLEMENTING HLL AND UTILITY TAPE ACCESS
!  FACILITIES TOGETHER IS TO COORDINATE THE REQUESTS TO DIRECTOR
!  FOR TAPE TRANSFERS.  THE DIRECTOR FACILITIES USED ARE THE
!  'DMAG CLAIM' AND 'DMAGIO' INTERFACES.  ALL CALLS ON THESE
!  DIRECTOR ROUTINES FROM THE HLL AND UTILITY INTERFACES ARE
!  ROUTED THROUGH A COMMON SET OF ROUTINES, THE 'TAPE SERVICE
!  ROUTINES'

!  THESE 'TAPE SERVICE ROUTINES' PERFORM VERY LITTLE CHECKING
!  OF THEIR OWN BUT ASSUME THAT MOST OF THE NECESSARY VALIDATION
!  OF PARAMETERS ETC HAS BEEN CARRIED OUT AT A HIGHER LEVEL SINCE
!  THE DEGREE OF CHECKING IS NOT NECESSARILY THE SAME FOR HLL AND
!  UTILITY ACCESS.  THESE ROUTINES PROVIDE TAPE HANDLING
!  PRIMITIVES THAT ARE FUNCTIONALLY VERY SIMILAR TO THE 'MAG'
!  ROUTINES.

!?2 removal of all lines beginiing '!?' turns this into SUBARC:S22.S
!?2 TO ASSIST WITH DIAGNOSING FAULTS IN THIS CODE, SOME TRACING
!?2 AND DIAGNOSTIC CODE HAS BEEN INCLUDED.  MOST OF THE STATEMENTS
!?2 INVOLVED IN THIS HAVE BEEN MARKED WITH THE SEQUENCE OF CHARACTERS
!?2 !?N WHERE N TAKES VARIOUS VALUES.  THIS IS TO ENABLE THE STRIPPING
!?2 OUT OF VARIOUS CATEGORIES OF DIAGNOSTIC CODE WHEN THEY ARE
!?2 NOT REQUIRED.  THE CATEGORIES INDICATED BY THE VARIOUS
!?2 VALUES OF N ARE LOOSELY DEFINED AS:
!?2 
!?2      1  TEMPORARY DIAGS FOR CHASING ERRORS
!?2      2  GENERALLY REQUIRED BY OTHER CATEGORIES
!?2      3  CHANNEL ALLOCATION AND USE
!?2      4  RECORD I/O TRACING
!?2      5  UNEXPECTED RESULTS FROM CALLS ON DIRECTOR INTERFACES
!?2

!**********************************************************************

!               REQUIRED DIRECTOR INTERFACE ROUTINES

!**********************************************************************

%externalintegerfnspec dmag claim(%stringname tsn,%integername sno,req,mode)
%externalintegerfnspec dmag io(%integername reply,control,len,type,sno,adr)
!  The various values that can be returned by DMAGIO in the REPLY FLAG
!  parameter should be interpreted as follows:
!  FLAG = 0: Request completed sucessfully,  For read check requests
!      CONTROL will hold the number of retries.
!  FLAG = 1: Thsi means one of the following:
!    Parity failure on read after 15 retries
!    * Read-after-write failure after 6 write retries
!    * Unmasked long block condition on read and in this case
!      CONTROL will bew set to 2 and LEN will contain the transfered length
!      which will inevitably be the requested length.
!    * Unmasked short block condition on read in which case
!      CONTROL will be set to 1 and LEN will contain the transfered
!      length which will be the length of the short block.
!  FLAG = 2: This has to be interpreted in conjuction with the value
!      opf the CONTROL parameter:
!    CONTROL = 8: Deck already busy, possibly due to some
!       badly behaved private chain etc.
!    CONTROL = 4: Service number not found due to tape not having been
!        claimed or tape not on deck etc.
!    CONTROL = 2: Deck not claimed or previously gone off line and
!        been remounted.
!    CONTROL = 1: Bad parameters.
!  FLAG = 3: Disaster - lost the tape or lost position on the tape, eg.
!   * Deck has been RESET or has failed mechanically.
!   * SKIP or REWIND has failed
!   * Requested transfer has failed and position on the tape has been lost.
!  FLAG = 4:  Unexpected BT, ET, tape mark or double tape mark.
!
%externalintegerfnspec dsfi(%stringname user,%integername fsys,type,set, %c
                            %stringname s,%integerarrayname ia)
!
!**********************************************************************

!              REQUIRED SUBSYSTEM ROUTINES

!**********************************************************************

